<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Shimbra Kure</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1529</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Shimbra-Kure · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-adal-war">Ethiopian–Adal War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Shimbra Kure was fought in March 1529 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-highlands">Ethiopian highlands</a>, where the forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-ibrahim-al-ghazi">Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Ghazi</a> routed a much larger army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>. Ahmad's victory rested on Ottoman-supplied firearms and disciplined use of them. It shattered the regional military balance and opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> to years of Adalite conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-shimbra-kure.jpg" alt="Battle of Shimbra Kure" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richard Pankhurst · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustration_of_Ahmad_Gragn_at_war.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
